{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:a64933e0a5da3372","name":"Personal Translator","source":{"id":"source:reference-a64933e0a5da3372","title":"Personal Translator","revision":21405,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:44:42Z","sha256":"bde0329f6ce43a2a14ee0343a11cf917191128277e6ab5158c17ddac8ae94dc5","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21405","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Personal%20Translator&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-a64933e0a5da3372","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 2,000\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 0.1 Kilograms\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Drawing from the successes of many Protocol Droids, the designers at Cybot Galactica condense the translating abilities of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["3PO-Series Protocol Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/3PO-Series_Protocol_Droid","referenceId":"reference:0cbde42806fd4d2c"}," into a tiny shell that can be worn around a person's neck or carried in a pocket. Thus, a person can carry a Personal Translator unit anywhere without having to rely on a Protocol Droid. The universal translator can translate verbal communications in the owner's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Language"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Language"}," and up to three other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Languages"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Languages","referenceId":"reference:318655cea4bd2096"}," of the owner's choosing. The device operates at the level of a DC 10 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Translator Unit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Translator_Unit","referenceId":"reference:0bcd4b383b11cac0"},". The translator has no photo receptors or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Appendages"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Appendages"},", so it is not able to interpret nonverbal forms of communication such as sign language.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
